eduka-language-pack-tet (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * LXQt: complete draft Tetun translation of all LXQt components (57 Qt
    catalogs, 3,677/3,706 messages) generated from the templates of LXQt
    master and the 2.1.x releases in Debian 13; installed where each
    component looks. New scripts/generate_lxqt.py and data/lxqt-tm.json.
  * Add upstream/lxqt-patches: QLocale-aware QTranslator::load() for liblxqt,
    lxqt-build-tools, libfm-qt, PCManFM-Qt, LXImage-Qt, QTerminal, qps,
    pavucontrol-qt, LXQt Archiver and ObConf-Qt (Qt reports "tet" as "C").
    Verified against Qt 6.4; replaces the old liblxqt raw-locale patch.
  * eduka-tet enable --desktop lxqt now sets LANG/LANGUAGE/LC_* in
    ~/.config/lxqt/session.conf [Environment] (reversible, journaled).
  * Add an Openbox gettext catalog (93/94 messages).
  * Correct 45 glossary entries (dez- prefix, accents, -iu endings,
    Portuguese function words, progressive "hela", word order) and apply the
    corrections to every catalog; see docs/CORRECTIONS.md.
  * Fix 9 native catalog entries that dropped a trailing space.
  * Add scripts/check_tetun.py (placeholders, accelerators, HTML tags,
    punctuation and spelling rules), run by make check and the tests.
  * QM compiler: accept single-form numerus messages.

 -- Hugo Moniz do Rego <ideaofficial@fdsl.tl>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

eduka-language-pack-tet (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging rewritten to follow Debian Policy and debhelper conventions:
    - debian/rules now uses dh with debhelper-compat 13 instead of a custom
      dpkg-deb script; the upstream Makefile is the single install path.
    - Documentation, examples and the manual page are installed with
      dh_installdocs, dh_installexamples and dh_installman; license texts are
      no longer duplicated in /usr/share/doc (see debian/copyright).
    - Add Vcs-*, Multi-Arch: foreign and ${misc:Depends}; list the covered
      desktops in the package description.
    - Maintainer scripts handle every dpkg action, include #DEBHELPER#, and
      remove the generated tet_TL.utf8 locale on remove as well as purge.
      A failed locale compilation now warns instead of breaking dpkg.
  * Install the .desktop file, icon and LXQt menu catalog from `make install`
    too, so source installs match the Debian package.
  * Mark bin/eduka-tet executable in git (tests failed on a fresh clone) and
    stop writing Python bytecode under /usr/share.
  * debian/copyright: set the real Source URL and drop build-only paths.
  * Add .gitignore and a GitHub Actions workflow that builds the package and
    runs lintian and an install/remove/purge test in Debian 13.

 -- Hugo Moniz do Rego <ideaofficial@fdsl.tl>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

eduka-language-pack-tet (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add 13 partial native GTK and desktop application catalogs with exact
    upstream message contexts, source hashes, copyright notices and licenses.
  * Expand the original community glossary to 432 draft terms.
  * Add reversible profile and Plasma settings, optional AccountsService
    integration for GNOME/GDM, XDG paths, conflict checks and a session journal.
  * Document all requested desktop families and GNU/Linux portability limits.
  * Record the three supplied dictionaries as permission-required references;
    do not redistribute their protected contents or claim INL endorsement.

 -- Hugo Moniz do Rego <ideaofficial@fdsl.tl>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

eduka-language-pack-tet (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial community draft: target-compiled Tetun locale, 315 original
